align:align-c-0001 a ev:ClaimAlignment ;
    rdfs:label "mott6-c-0060 vs shigley10-c-0060"@en ;
    mdcore:analystNote "Both books state that a key can fail by direct shear or by bearing (compressive) stress, and both treat the two as checks to be made together. No difference in scope or condition."@en ;
    mdcore:reviewStatus mdcore:NeedsReview ;
    ev:alignmentType ev:Agrees ;
    ev:commonConcept "failure modes of a key transmitting torque"@en ;
    ev:sourceClaimA mott6:c-0060 ;
    ev:sourceClaimB shigley10:c-0060 .

align:align-c-0002 a ev:ClaimAlignment ;
    rdfs:label "mott6-c-0071 vs shigley10-c-0074"@en ;
    mdcore:analystNote "Agreement to within the rounding Mott applies. The remaining 0.1 percent difference in the roller exponent is a rounding artefact, not a disagreement, and is preserved rather than normalised away."@en ;
    mdcore:reviewStatus mdcore:NeedsReview ;
    ev:alignmentType ev:Agrees ;
    ev:commonConcept "rolling-bearing load/life exponent"@en ;
    ev:differingConditions "For ball bearings the values are identical (3.00 and 3). For roller bearings Mott prints 3.33 while Shigley prints the exact fraction 10/3 (3.3333...); Shigley additionally states the value applies to cylindrical and tapered roller bearings, whereas Mott says only 'roller bearings'."@en ;
    ev:sourceClaimA mott6:c-0071 ;
    ev:sourceClaimB shigley10:c-0074 .

align:align-c-0003 a ev:ClaimAlignment ;
    rdfs:label "mott6-c-0070 vs shigley10-c-0074"@en ;
    mdcore:analystNote "Algebraically the same relation. Shigley's form makes the 0.90 reliability attachment explicit, which Mott's ratio form leaves implicit."@en ;
    mdcore:reviewStatus mdcore:NeedsReview ;
    ev:alignmentType ev:CloseMatch ;
    ev:commonConcept "load-life power law for rolling bearings"@en ;
    ev:differingAssumptions "Mott writes the law as a ratio between two operating points, which cancels the rating-life basis; Shigley writes it as an invariant of a regression line explicitly associated with reliability 0.90."@en ;
    ev:sourceClaimA mott6:c-0070 ;
    ev:sourceClaimB shigley10:c-0074 .

align:align-c-0004 a ev:ClaimAlignment ;
    rdfs:label "mott6-c-0074 vs shigley10-c-0073"@en ;
    mdcore:analystNote "Practically important. Applying Mott's C = P_d (L_d/10^6)^(1/k) to a catalogue rated on a different basis gives a wrong answer. Shigley's claim refines and bounds Mott's assumption; both are kept."@en ;
    mdcore:reviewStatus mdcore:NeedsReview ;
    ev:alignmentType ev:Refines ;
    ev:commonConcept "catalogue rating-life basis"@en ;
    ev:differingAssumptions "Mott's working equations assume the manufacturer's data are rated at 10^6 revolutions. Shigley states that this is merely the most common basis and names a well-known manufacturer that rates at 3000 hours at 500 rev/min, equal to 90 million revolutions."@en ;
    ev:sourceClaimA mott6:c-0074 ;
    ev:sourceClaimB shigley10:c-0073 .

align:align-c-0005 a ev:ClaimAlignment ;
    rdfs:label "mott6-c-0041 vs shigley10-c-0041"@en ;
    mdcore:analystNote "Not a contradiction. The books foreground different evaluation criteria and different design situations. Merging them into a single verdict on splines would destroy exactly the information a designer needs. Both are retained and the substitution assessments cite both."@en ;
    mdcore:reviewStatus mdcore:NeedsReview ;
    ev:alignmentType ev:DiffersInScope ;
    ev:commonConcept "splines compared with keys"@en ;
    ev:differingConditions "Mott's 'many advantages' is asserted on load sharing, integral construction, controlled fit, wear resistance and indexing. Shigley's 'usually not necessary' is asserted on manufacturing cost, for the specific case of simple torque transmission."@en ;
    ev:sourceClaimA mott6:c-0041 ;
    ev:sourceClaimB shigley10:c-0041 .

align:align-c-0006 a ev:ClaimAlignment ;
    rdfs:label "mott6-c-0063 vs shigley10-c-0024"@en ;
    mdcore:analystNote "The two are not formally contradictory: Mott gives a number, Shigley gives a direction, and N = 3 is not necessarily 'excessive'. But they express opposite design intents -- survive the overload versus act as the fuse -- and which applies depends on whether the key is meant to be sacrificial. Left explicitly unresolved. Any rule derived from either must state which intent it assumes."@en ;
    mdcore:reviewStatus mdcore:NeedsReview ;
    ev:alignmentType ev:DiffersInAssumption ;
    ev:commonConcept "how conservative a key design should be"@en ;
    ev:differingAssumptions "Mott's parallel-key design procedure recommends N = 3 in typical industrial applications, explicitly to accommodate accidental overloads and shock. Shigley warns that excessive safety factors should be avoided in key design because it is desirable for the key, rather than costlier components, to fail in an overload."@en ;
    ev:sourceClaimA mott6:c-0063 ;
    ev:sourceClaimB shigley10:c-0024 .

align:align-c-0007 a ev:ClaimAlignment ;
    rdfs:label "mott6-c-0044 vs shigley10-c-0043"@en ;
    mdcore:analystNote "Mott states that sliding motion between a standard parallel key and the mating element should not be permitted; Shigley states that a spline with a loose slip fit allows large axial motion while still transmitting torque. Together they establish, from two independent sources, the condition under which a key cannot be used and a spline can. This pair is the evidential basis of substitution assessment SA-001."@en ;
    mdcore:reviewStatus mdcore:NeedsReview ;
    ev:alignmentType ev:Complements ;
    ev:commonConcept "axial motion of a hub relative to the shaft while torque is transmitted"@en ;
    ev:sourceClaimA mott6:c-0044 ;
    ev:sourceClaimB shigley10:c-0043 .

align:align-c-0008 a ev:ClaimAlignment ;
    rdfs:label "mott6-c-0049 vs shigley10-c-0023"@en ;
    mdcore:analystNote "Mott offers two keys or a spline as the remedy when a single key would be longer than the hub. Shigley states that multiple keys may be used to carry greater loads and adds the practical detail that they are typically oriented at 90 degrees apart. Shigley supplies the arrangement Mott omits."@en ;
    mdcore:reviewStatus mdcore:NeedsReview ;
    ev:alignmentType ev:Complements ;
    ev:commonConcept "using more than one key to carry a larger load"@en ;
    ev:sourceClaimA mott6:c-0049 ;
    ev:sourceClaimB shigley10:c-0023 .

align:align-c-0009 a ev:ClaimAlignment ;
    rdfs:label "mott6-c-0001 vs shigley10-c-0001"@en ;
    mdcore:analystNote "Both define the design factor as the ratio of a strength to an allowable stress, and both derive a design stress by dividing strength by the factor."@en ;
    mdcore:reviewStatus mdcore:NeedsReview ;
    ev:alignmentType ev:Agrees ;
    ev:commonConcept "definition of the design factor"@en ;
    ev:sourceClaimA mott6:c-0001 ;
    ev:sourceClaimB shigley10:c-0001 .

align:align-c-0010 a ev:ClaimAlignment ;
    rdfs:label "mott6-c-0001 vs shigley10-c-0002"@en ;
    mdcore:analystNote "A reader combining formulas from both books must check which of the two roles each symbol plays; they are not blindly interchangeable."@en ;
    mdcore:reviewStatus mdcore:NeedsReview ;
    ev:alignmentType ev:DiffersInTerminology ;
    ev:commonConcept "naming of the safety margin before and after design"@en ;
    ev:differingConditions "Shigley separates n_d (chosen) from n (achieved). Mott uses N for both roles."@en ;
    ev:sourceClaimA mott6:c-0001 ;
    ev:sourceClaimB shigley10:c-0002 .

align:align-c-0011 a ev:ClaimAlignment ;
    rdfs:label "mott6-c-0025 vs shigley10-c-0026"@en ;
    mdcore:analystNote "Non-overlapping rationales for the same element. Taken together they give a fuller applicability profile than either book alone."@en ;
    mdcore:reviewStatus mdcore:NeedsReview ;
    ev:alignmentType ev:Complements ;
    ev:commonConcept "when to choose a Woodruff key"@en ;
    ev:differingConditions "Mott's stated conditions are light loading and easy assembly and disassembly. Shigley's are concentricity after assembly, positioning against a shoulder without cutting the keyslot into the stress concentration region, and prevention of key rolling in smaller shafts."@en ;
    ev:sourceClaimA mott6:c-0025 ;
    ev:sourceClaimB shigley10:c-0026 .

align:align-c-0012 a ev:ClaimAlignment ;
    rdfs:label "mott6-c-0053 vs shigley10-c-0046"@en ;
    mdcore:analystNote "Mott states that pin-type connections produce stress concentrations in the shaft; Shigley states that the stress-concentration factor from a press or shrink fit is usually quite small. Read together they support a comparative ranking, which neither book states outright. Any such ranking is an analyst inference and is marked as one."@en ;
    mdcore:reviewStatus mdcore:NeedsReview ;
    ev:alignmentType ev:Complements ;
    ev:commonConcept "stress concentration introduced by a shaft/hub connection"@en ;
    ev:sourceClaimA mott6:c-0053 ;
    ev:sourceClaimB shigley10:c-0046 .

align:align-c-0013 a ev:ClaimAlignment ;
    rdfs:label "mott6-c-0076 vs shigley10-c-0073"@en ;
    mdcore:analystNote "Both books direct the designer to manufacturer data for any real bearing selection, and both present their own tabulated values as illustrative."@en ;
    mdcore:reviewStatus mdcore:NeedsReview ;
    ev:alignmentType ev:Agrees ;
    ev:commonConcept "necessity of using the specific manufacturer's published data"@en ;
    ev:sourceClaimA mott6:c-0076 ;
    ev:sourceClaimB shigley10:c-0073 .

align:align-c-0014 a ev:ClaimAlignment ;
    rdfs:label "mott6-c-0047 vs shigley10-c-0042"@en ;
    mdcore:analystNote "Complementary in practice but not comparable as statements: one is quantitative and narrow, the other qualitative and broad. Only Mott's claim can support a capacity calculation, and only within its stated unit system."@en ;
    mdcore:reviewStatus mdcore:NeedsReview ;
    ev:alignmentType ev:DiffersInScope ;
    ev:commonConcept "torque capacity of a spline connection"@en ;
    ev:differingConditions "Mott supplies a closed-form capacity model for SAE straight-sided splines based on a 1000 psi allowable bearing stress, in inch units. Shigley states only that splines are typically used to transfer high torques and gives no spline capacity equation in the cited section."@en ;
    ev:sourceClaimA mott6:c-0047 ;
    ev:sourceClaimB shigley10:c-0042 .

align:align-c-0015 a ev:ClaimAlignment ;
    rdfs:label "mott6-c-0073 vs shigley10-c-0070"@en ;
    mdcore:analystNote "Mott gives the physical reason (fatigue under high contact stress); Shigley gives the statistical definition of the life that is quoted (the 10th percentile of the failure distribution). Neither is complete alone."@en ;
    mdcore:reviewStatus mdcore:NeedsReview ;
    ev:alignmentType ev:Complements ;
    ev:commonConcept "why rolling bearings have a finite life"@en ;
    ev:sourceClaimA mott6:c-0073 ;
    ev:sourceClaimB shigley10:c-0070 .

align:align-t-0001 a ev:TerminologyAlignment ;
    rdfs:label "design factor"@en ;
    mdcore:analystNote "Both denote the ratio by which strength exceeds the stress or load a part must carry. Symbols differ. Shigley additionally reserves a second symbol for the value actually achieved after design; Mott does not."@en ;
    mdcore:reviewStatus mdcore:NeedsReview ;
    ev:alignmentType ev:CloseMatch ;
    ev:alignsSourceSymbol "mott6: N",
        "shigley10: n_d" ;
    ev:alignsSourceTerm "mott6: design factor"@en,
        "shigley10: design factor"@en ;
    ev:alignsToConcept mdcore:SafetyRequirement ;
    ev:commonConcept "design factor"@en ;
    ev:supportedByEvidence mott6:es-0001,
        shigley10:es-0001 .

align:align-t-0002 a ev:TerminologyAlignment ;
    rdfs:label "achieved safety margin after the design is fixed"@en ;
    mdcore:analystNote "Shigley distinguishes the a-priori design factor n_d from the as-built factor of safety n, which generally differs numerically because of rounding to standard sizes. Mott uses one symbol N throughout. Readers moving between the books must not assume N and n are interchangeable."@en ;
    mdcore:reviewStatus mdcore:NeedsReview ;
    ev:alignmentType ev:DiffersInTerminology ;
    ev:alignsSourceSymbol "mott6: N",
        "shigley10: n" ;
    ev:alignsSourceTerm "mott6: design factor (no separate term)"@en,
        "shigley10: factor of safety"@en ;
    ev:alignsToConcept mdcore:SafetyRequirement ;
    ev:commonConcept "achieved safety margin after the design is fixed"@en ;
    ev:supportedByEvidence mott6:es-0001,
        shigley10:es-0002 .

align:align-t-0003 a ev:TerminologyAlignment ;
    rdfs:label "rolling-bearing load/life exponent"@en ;
    mdcore:analystNote "Same physical exponent, different symbol. Values agree for ball bearings (3.00 and 3); for roller bearings Mott prints the rounded decimal 3.33 and Shigley the exact fraction 10/3. The symbols are deliberately NOT merged in the graph."@en ;
    mdcore:reviewStatus mdcore:NeedsReview ;
    ev:alignmentType ev:ExactMatch ;
    ev:alignsSourceSymbol "mott6: k",
        "shigley10: a" ;
    ev:alignsSourceTerm "mott6: load/life exponent"@en,
        "shigley10: load-life exponent"@en ;
    ev:alignsToConcept mech:BearingLifeCalculation ;
    ev:commonConcept "rolling-bearing load/life exponent"@en ;
    ev:supportedByEvidence mott6:es-0071,
        shigley10:es-0054 .

align:align-t-0004 a ev:TerminologyAlignment ;
    rdfs:label "load applied to a rolling bearing"@en ;
    mdcore:analystNote "Same quantity, different symbol. Note the collision risk: Shigley uses P elsewhere for force, pressure and diametral pitch, so symbol-level merging across the two books would be actively wrong."@en ;
    mdcore:reviewStatus mdcore:NeedsReview ;
    ev:alignmentType ev:DiffersInTerminology ;
    ev:alignsSourceSymbol "mott6: P",
        "shigley10: F" ;
    ev:alignsSourceTerm "mott6: load"@en,
        "shigley10: load"@en ;
    ev:alignsToConcept mdcore:LoadCapacityRequirement ;
    ev:commonConcept "load applied to a rolling bearing"@en ;
    ev:supportedByEvidence mott6:es-0070,
        shigley10:es-0054 .

align:align-t-0005 a ev:TerminologyAlignment ;
    rdfs:label "load-life relation for rolling bearings"@en ;
    mdcore:analystNote "Algebraically equivalent statements of the same power law, written in different forms: Mott as a ratio between two operating points, Shigley as an invariant of the fitted line. Equivalence holds only when the exponent and the rating-life basis are matched."@en ;
    mdcore:reviewStatus mdcore:NeedsReview ;
    ev:alignmentType ev:CloseMatch ;
    ev:alignsSourceSymbol "mott6: Eq. 14-1",
        "shigley10: Eq. 11-1" ;
    ev:alignsSourceTerm "mott6: relationship between bearing load and life, L2/L1 = (P1/P2)^k"@en,
        "shigley10: load-life regression, F L^(1/a) = constant"@en ;
    ev:alignsToConcept mech:BearingLifeCalculation ;
    ev:commonConcept "load-life relation for rolling bearings"@en ;
    ev:supportedByEvidence mott6:es-0070,
        shigley10:es-0054 .

align:align-t-0006 a ev:TerminologyAlignment ;
    rdfs:label "rating life at 90 percent survival"@en ;
    mdcore:analystNote "Shigley gives the fuller definition, attributes the term to the ABMA, enumerates the synonyms, and locates it as the 10th percentile of the revolutions-to-failure distribution. Shigley refines Mott here rather than disagreeing with it."@en ;
    mdcore:reviewStatus mdcore:NeedsReview ;
    ev:alignmentType ev:Refines ;
    ev:alignsSourceSymbol "mott6: L10",
        "shigley10: L10" ;
    ev:alignsSourceTerm "mott6: rated life / L10 life"@en,
        "shigley10: rating life (also minimum life, L10 life, B10 life)"@en ;
    ev:alignsToConcept mdcore:LifeRequirement ;
    ev:commonConcept "rating life at 90 percent survival"@en ;
    ev:supportedByEvidence mott6:es-0070,
        shigley10:es-0050,
        shigley10:es-0051 .

align:align-t-0007 a ev:TerminologyAlignment ;
    rdfs:label "basic dynamic load rating"@en ;
    mdcore:analystNote "Shigley's subscript 10 marks the tie to the 10 percent failure fraction, and Shigley notes the name Basic Dynamic Load Rating applies specifically when the manufacturer's rating life is one million revolutions. Mott's C carries the same meaning but assumes that basis silently."@en ;
    mdcore:reviewStatus mdcore:NeedsReview ;
    ev:alignmentType ev:CloseMatch ;
    ev:alignsSourceSymbol "mott6: C",
        "shigley10: C10" ;
    ev:alignsSourceTerm "mott6: basic dynamic load rating"@en,
        "shigley10: catalog load rating / Basic Dynamic Load Rating"@en ;
    ev:alignsToConcept melem:RollingContactBearing ;
    ev:commonConcept "basic dynamic load rating"@en ;
    ev:supportedByEvidence mott6:es-0072,
        shigley10:es-0055 .

align:align-t-0008 a ev:TerminologyAlignment ;
    rdfs:label "groove receiving a key"@en ;
    mdcore:analystNote "Mott explicitly notes that the hub groove is usually called a keyway but is more properly also a keyseat. The ontology keeps one class and records both surface forms as labels rather than picking a winner."@en ;
    mdcore:reviewStatus mdcore:NeedsReview ;
    ev:alignmentType ev:DiffersInTerminology ;
    ev:alignsSourceTerm "mott6: keyseat (shaft and hub); keyway used commonly for the hub groove"@en,
        "shigley10: keyseat; keyway depth"@en ;
    ev:alignsToConcept mech:Keyseat ;
    ev:commonConcept "groove receiving a key"@en ;
    ev:supportedByEvidence mott6:es-0020,
        shigley10:es-0032 .

align:align-t-0009 a ev:TerminologyAlignment ;
    rdfs:label "spline"@en ;
    mdcore:analystNote "Same element, two framings. Mott frames the spline as a multiplied key, Shigley as a shortened gear. The framings foreshadow their differing emphases: Mott stresses load sharing, Shigley stresses manufacturing cost."@en ;
    mdcore:reviewStatus mdcore:NeedsReview ;
    ev:alignmentType ev:CloseMatch ;
    ev:alignsSourceTerm "mott6: a series of axial keys machined into a shaft, with corresponding grooves in the bore of the mating part"@en,
        "shigley10: essentially stubby gear teeth formed on the outside of the shaft and inside of the hub"@en ;
    ev:alignsToConcept melem:Spline ;
    ev:commonConcept "spline"@en ;
    ev:supportedByEvidence mott6:es-0040,
        shigley10:es-0010 .

align:align-t-0010 a ev:TerminologyAlignment ;
    rdfs:label "yield strength"@en ;
    mdcore:analystNote "Same property; Mott uses lower-case s for strengths and Shigley upper-case S. A purely notational difference, but one that breaks naive symbol matching across the two books."@en ;
    mdcore:reviewStatus mdcore:NeedsReview ;
    ev:alignmentType ev:ExactMatch ;
    ev:alignsSourceSymbol "mott6: s_y",
        "shigley10: S_y" ;
    ev:alignsSourceTerm "mott6: yield strength"@en,
        "shigley10: yield strength"@en ;
    ev:alignsToConcept mech:YieldStrength ;
    ev:commonConcept "yield strength"@en ;
    ev:supportedByEvidence mott6:es-0031,
        shigley10:es-0004 .

align:align-t-0011 a ev:TerminologyAlignment ;
    rdfs:label "failure modes of a key"@en ;
    mdcore:analystNote "The two books identify the same two failure modes for a key in the same order. One of the clearest agreements in the pilot."@en ;
    mdcore:reviewStatus mdcore:NeedsReview ;
    ev:alignmentType ev:ExactMatch ;
    ev:alignsSourceTerm "mott6: shear across the shaft/hub interface; compression due to bearing action"@en,
        "shigley10: direct shear; bearing stress"@en ;
    ev:alignsToConcept melem:ParallelKeyConnection ;
    ev:commonConcept "failure modes of a key"@en ;
    ev:supportedByEvidence mott6:es-0030,
        shigley10:es-0032 .

align:align-t-0012 a ev:TerminologyAlignment ;
    rdfs:label "torque capacity of a friction-based shaft/hub connection"@en ;
    mdcore:analystNote "Both concern friction-based torque transfer at a pressurised shaft/hub interface, but Shigley supplies a closed-form capacity model for a plain interference fit while Mott describes a proprietary ring assembly and directs the reader to the manufacturer. Not interchangeable as a basis for calculation."@en ;
    mdcore:reviewStatus mdcore:NeedsReview ;
    ev:alignmentType ev:RelatedNotEquivalent ;
    ev:alignsSourceSymbol "shigley10: Eq. 7-49" ;
    ev:alignsSourceTerm "mott6: keyless hub-to-shaft connection using a compressed steel ring (proprietary locking assembly)"@en,
        "shigley10: interference fit torque capacity, T = (pi/2) f p l d^2"@en ;
    ev:alignsToConcept mech:FrictionalLoadTransfer ;
    ev:commonConcept "torque capacity of a friction-based shaft/hub connection"@en ;
    ev:supportedByEvidence mott6:es-0065,
        shigley10:es-0041 .

mdcore:AnalyticalModel a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Analytical Model"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mdcore:CalculationMethod ;
    skos:definition "A derived model of behaviour, stated with its assumptions and validity conditions."@en .

mdcore:Assembly a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Assembly"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mdcore:DesignedArtifact ;
    skos:altLabel "조립체"@ko ;
    skos:definition """A designed artifact produced by joining two or more
        artifacts through interfaces, and which is handled as a single item at
        the next level of assembly."""@en .

mdcore:AssemblyEffortRequirement a mdcore:RequirementKind ;
    skos:inScheme mdcore:RequirementKindScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "assembly and disassembly effort"@en .

mdcore:AutomaticallyExtracted a mdcore:ReviewState ;
    skos:altLabel "자동 추출"@ko ;
    skos:inScheme mdcore:ReviewStateScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "automatically extracted"@en ;
    mdcore:ordinalRank 1 .

mdcore:AvailabilityConstraint a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Availability Constraint"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mdcore:EconomicCondition ;
    skos:definition "Constraint arising from procurement lead time or from whether an element is a standard, catalogue item."@en .

mdcore:ComputedResult a mdcore:ValueProvenanceKind ;
    skos:definition "Produced by the pipeline from other values; traceable to its inputs."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mdcore:ValueProvenanceScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "computed result"@en .

mdcore:Constraint a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Constraint"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mdcore:Requirement ;
    skos:altLabel "제약조건"@ko ;
    skos:definition """A requirement that bounds the admissible solution space
        rather than expressing a desired level of performance; it is satisfied
        or violated, and is not traded off."""@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Distinguishing Constraint from the general Requirement
        matters for decision-making: constraints filter the candidate set
        before any weighting or scoring is applied."""@en .

mdcore:ContaminatedEnvironment a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Contaminated Environment"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mdcore:EnvironmentalCondition .

mdcore:CorrosionResistanceRequirement a mdcore:RequirementKind ;
    skos:inScheme mdcore:RequirementKindScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "corrosion resistance"@en .

mdcore:CorrosiveEnvironment a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Corrosive Environment"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mdcore:EnvironmentalCondition ;
    skos:altLabel "부식 환경"@ko .

mdcore:DeflectionRequirement a mdcore:RequirementKind ;
    skos:inScheme mdcore:RequirementKindScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "deflection"@en .

mdcore:DirectlySubstitutable a mdcore:SubstitutionState ;
    skos:altLabel "직접 대체 가능"@ko ;
    skos:definition """The candidate can replace the baseline while preserving
        the required function, the interfaces, the operating conditions and the
        essential requirements, without significant redesign."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme mdcore:SubstitutionStateScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "directly substitutable"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Must never be inferred from a shared function. Requires
        positive evidence on interface compatibility and on the binding
        requirements."""@en .

mdcore:FatigueTest a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Fatigue Test"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mdcore:TestMethod .

mdcore:FrequentAssembly a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Frequent Assembly"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mdcore:AssemblyCondition .

mdcore:FrequentDisassembly a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Frequent Disassembly"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mdcore:MaintenanceCondition .

mdcore:FunctionalAlternative a mdcore:SubstitutionState ;
    skos:altLabel "기능적 대안"@ko ;
    skos:definition """Both alternatives can perform at least one common
        required function, but they are not thereby interchangeable."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme mdcore:SubstitutionStateScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "functional alternative"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """This is the strongest verdict that a shared function alone
        can justify."""@en .

mdcore:FunctionalTest a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Functional Test"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mdcore:TestMethod .

mdcore:HumanVerified a mdcore:ReviewState ;
    skos:altLabel "검증 완료"@ko ;
    skos:inScheme mdcore:ReviewStateScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "human verified"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Asserts that a named person compared the normalized
        statement against the cited page and accepted it."""@en ;
    mdcore:ordinalRank 4 .

mdcore:InspectabilityRequirement a mdcore:RequirementKind ;
    skos:inScheme mdcore:RequirementKindScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "inspectability"@en .

mdcore:InterfaceIdentical a mdcore:InterfaceCompatibilityLevel ;
    skos:definition "Mating geometry, tolerances and fit class are unchanged."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mdcore:InterfaceCompatibilityScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "interface identical"@en .

mdcore:LifeTest a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Life Test"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mdcore:TestMethod .

mdcore:LinearMotion a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Linear Motion"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mdcore:KinematicCondition ;
    skos:altLabel "직선운동"@ko .

mdcore:MaintenanceCostConstraint a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Maintenance Cost Constraint"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mdcore:EconomicCondition .

mdcore:ManufacturabilityRequirement a mdcore:RequirementKind ;
    skos:inScheme mdcore:RequirementKindScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "manufacturability"@en .

mdcore:ManufacturingCondition a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Manufacturing Condition"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mdcore:LifecycleCondition ;
    skos:altLabel "제조 조건"@ko .

mdcore:MassRequirement a mdcore:RequirementKind ;
    skos:inScheme mdcore:RequirementKindScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "mass"@en .

mdcore:MaterialInspection a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Material Inspection"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mdcore:InspectionMethod .

mdcore:NoiseRequirement a mdcore:RequirementKind ;
    skos:inScheme mdcore:RequirementKindScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "noise"@en .

mdcore:Normalized a mdcore:ReviewState ;
    skos:altLabel "정규화됨"@ko ;
    skos:inScheme mdcore:ReviewStateScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "normalized"@en ;
    mdcore:ordinalRank 2 .

mdcore:NumericalSimulation a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Numerical Simulation"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mdcore:SimulationMethod .

mdcore:OscillatingMotion a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Oscillating Motion"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mdcore:KinematicCondition .

mdcore:OverloadCondition a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Overload Condition"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mdcore:LoadingCondition ;
    skos:definition "An occasional load exceeding the nominal design load, whether accidental or inherent to the duty."@en .

mdcore:PowerCapacityRequirement a mdcore:RequirementKind ;
    skos:inScheme mdcore:RequirementKindScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "power capacity"@en .

mdcore:Rejected a mdcore:ReviewState ;
    skos:altLabel "기각됨"@ko ;
    skos:inScheme mdcore:ReviewStateScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "rejected"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Retained, not deleted, so that the same erroneous extraction is not re-proposed."@en ;
    mdcore:ordinalRank 0 .

mdcore:RequiredServiceLife a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Required Service Life"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mdcore:LifecycleCondition .

mdcore:SatisfactionUnknown a mdcore:SatisfactionLevel ;
    skos:altLabel "불명"@ko ;
    skos:definition "Neither the sources nor the analyst can determine the level. Distinct from 'does not satisfy'."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mdcore:SatisfactionScale ;
    skos:prefLabel "unknown"@en .

mdcore:SelectionCriterion a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Selection Criterion"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mdcore:EvaluationCriterion ;
    skos:definition """An evaluation criterion used to choose among admissible
        alternatives, as opposed to one used to screen them for
        admissibility."""@en .

mdcore:StiffnessRequirement a mdcore:RequirementKind ;
    skos:inScheme mdcore:RequirementKindScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "stiffness"@en .

mdcore:TemperatureCondition a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Temperature Condition"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mdcore:EnvironmentalCondition .

mdcore:TemperatureResistanceRequirement a mdcore:RequirementKind ;
    skos:inScheme mdcore:RequirementKindScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "temperature resistance"@en .

mdcore:TemperatureTest a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Temperature Test"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mdcore:TestMethod .

mdcore:Unit a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Unit"@en ;
    skos:definition """A unit of measure. Identified by a symbol string; the
        pipeline validates dimensional consistency with Pint rather than by
        OWL reasoning."""@en .

mdcore:UserDefinedWeight a mdcore:ValueProvenanceKind ;
    skos:definition "A preference supplied by the user of the decision model."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mdcore:ValueProvenanceScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "user-defined weight"@en .

mdcore:VibrationRequirement a mdcore:RequirementKind ;
    skos:inScheme mdcore:RequirementKindScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "vibration"@en .

mdcore:VibrationTest a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Vibration Test"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mdcore:TestMethod .

mdcore:acceptanceCriterionSpecified a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "acceptance criterion specified by source"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:VerificationMethod ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean .

mdcore:acceptanceStatement a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "acceptance statement"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:AcceptanceCriterion ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mdcore:acceptanceThreshold a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "acceptance threshold"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:AcceptanceCriterion ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:QuantityValue .

mdcore:addressesFailureMode a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "addresses failure mode"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:VerificationMethod ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:FailureMode .

mdcore:againstCriterion a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "against criterion"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:AlternativeEvaluation ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:EvaluationCriterion .

mdcore:aggravatedByCondition a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "aggravated by condition"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:FailureMode ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:OperatingCondition .

mdcore:analystNote a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "analyst note"@en ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    skos:scopeNote "Explicitly the analyst's voice. Never quotable as source content."@en .

mdcore:applicableContext a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "applicable in operating context"@en ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:OperatingContext .

mdcore:applicableRequirement a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "applicable requirement"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:SubstitutionAssessment ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:Requirement .

mdcore:assessmentAdvantage a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "advantage of substituting"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:SubstitutionAssessment ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:AlternativeEvaluation .

mdcore:assessmentConclusion a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "assessment conclusion"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:SubstitutionAssessment ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:SubstitutionState .

mdcore:assessmentCondition a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "substitution condition"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:SubstitutionAssessment ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:OperatingCondition ;
    skos:definition "A condition that must hold for the conclusion to apply."@en .

mdcore:assessmentContext a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "assessment operating context"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:SubstitutionAssessment ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:OperatingContext .

mdcore:assessmentDisadvantage a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "disadvantage of substituting"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:SubstitutionAssessment ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:AlternativeEvaluation .

mdcore:assessmentTradeOff a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "trade-off of substituting"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:SubstitutionAssessment ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:TradeOff .

mdcore:baselineAlternative a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "baseline alternative"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:SubstitutionAssessment ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:DesignAlternative ;
    skos:definition "The alternative currently assumed, which the candidate would displace."@en .

mdcore:behaviorRequiresCondition a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "behavior requires condition"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:Behavior ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:OperatingCondition ;
    skos:definition """A condition that must hold for the behavior to occur at
        all, for example a maintained normal pressure for a friction-based
        load transfer."""@en .

mdcore:candidateAlternative a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "candidate alternative"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:SubstitutionAssessment ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:DesignAlternative ;
    skos:definition "The alternative proposed as a replacement."@en .

mdcore:candidateSetFor a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "candidate set for problem"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:CandidateSet ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:DesignProblem .

mdcore:causedByFailureMechanism a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "caused by failure mechanism"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:FailureMode ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:FailureMechanism .

mdcore:conditionParameter a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "condition parameter"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:OperatingCondition ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:QuantityValue ;
    skos:definition "A quantified parameter of the condition, with its unit."@en .

mdcore:conditionStatement a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "condition statement"@en ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    skos:scopeNote "Human-readable restatement. Never the only representation: a structured condition must also be given."@en .

mdcore:confidence a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "confidence"@en ;
    rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
    skos:scopeNote "In [0,1]. An analyst's or extractor's stated confidence, never a probability derived from data unless the source supplied one."@en .

mdcore:connects a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "connects"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:Interface ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:DesignedArtifact ;
    skos:definition "Relates an interface to each artifact it joins."@en .

mdcore:contextUnspecified a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "context deliberately unspecified"@en ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    skos:definition """Explicit marker that a statement's applicable context is
        not stated by its source. Forces the absence of context to be a
        recorded fact rather than an oversight."""@en .

mdcore:conversionMethod a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "conversion method"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:QuantityValue ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    skos:scopeNote "For example 'pint 0.24; 1 psi = 6894.757 Pa; exact'. Required whenever normalizedValue differs from numericValue."@en .

mdcore:decidesProblem a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "decides problem"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DesignDecision ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:DesignProblem .

mdcore:decomposesFunction a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "decomposes function"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:FunctionDecomposition ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:Function .

mdcore:definesTerm a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "defines qualitative term"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:ThresholdDefinition ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mdcore:derivedFromRequirement a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "derived from requirement"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:EvaluationCriterion ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:Requirement .

mdcore:enablesBehavior a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "enables behavior"@en ;
    owl:inverseOf mdcore:enabledBy .

mdcore:evaluatesAlternative a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "evaluates alternative"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:AlternativeEvaluation ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:DesignAlternative .

mdcore:evaluationLevel a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "evaluation level"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:AlternativeEvaluation ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:SatisfactionLevel .

mdcore:evaluationQuantity a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "evaluation numeric value"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:AlternativeEvaluation ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:QuantityValue ;
    skos:scopeNote """Present only when the source printed a number, or when the
        value is explicitly marked as an analyst-defined decision-model value
        via mdcore:valueProvenance."""@en .

mdcore:evaluationScale a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "evaluation scale"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:AlternativeEvaluation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    skos:scopeNote "Names the scale used, e.g. 'mdkg qualitative satisfaction scale v1' or 'lbf'."@en .

mdcore:exclusionRationale a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "exclusion rationale"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:CandidateSet ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mdcore:functionBeingPreserved a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "function being preserved"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:SubstitutionAssessment ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:Function ;
    skos:scopeNote """Mandatory. Substitution claims that do not say what is
        being preserved are not interpretable."""@en .

mdcore:hasAcceptanceCriterion a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has acceptance criterion"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:VerificationMethod ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:AcceptanceCriterion .

mdcore:hasAdvantage a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has advantage"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DesignAlternative ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:AlternativeEvaluation ;
    skos:scopeNote "Points at an evaluation so that the advantage carries its context and provenance, rather than being a bare string."@en .

mdcore:hasCandidate a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has candidate"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:CandidateSet ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:DesignAlternative .

mdcore:hasCondition a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has condition"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:OperatingContext ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:OperatingCondition .

mdcore:hasConsequence a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has failure consequence"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:FailureMode ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:FailureConsequence .

mdcore:hasDesignFeature a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has design feature"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DesignedArtifact ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:DesignFeature .

mdcore:hasDisadvantage a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has disadvantage"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DesignAlternative ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:AlternativeEvaluation .

mdcore:hasGeometryFeature a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has geometry feature"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DesignedArtifact ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:GeometryFeature .

mdcore:hasInterface a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has interface"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DesignedArtifact ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:Interface .

mdcore:hasRationale a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has rationale"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DesignDecision ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:DecisionRationale .

mdcore:hasRequirement a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has requirement"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DesignProblem ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:Requirement .

mdcore:hasRequirementKind a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has requirement kind"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:Requirement ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:RequirementKind .

mdcore:hasSubFunction a owl:ObjectProperty,
        owl:TransitiveProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has sub-function"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:Function ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:Function .

mdcore:hasTargetValue a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has target value"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:Requirement ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:QuantityValue .

mdcore:initiatesAtFeature a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "initiates at geometry feature"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:FailureMode ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:GeometryFeature ;
    skos:definition "The geometry feature at which the failure characteristically starts, such as a keyseat or a fillet."@en .

mdcore:interfaceCompatibility a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "interface compatibility"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:SubstitutionAssessment ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:InterfaceCompatibilityLevel .

mdcore:introducedFailureMode a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "failure mode introduced by candidate"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:SubstitutionAssessment ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:FailureMode .

mdcore:isProtectiveFailure a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "is protective (sacrificial) failure"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:FailureMode ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    skos:definition """True when the failure of this element is deliberately
        preferred to the failure of adjacent, costlier components."""@en .

mdcore:madeOfMaterial a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "made of material"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DesignedArtifact ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:Material .

mdcore:mayExperienceFailureMode a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "may experience failure mode"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DesignAlternative ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:FailureMode ;
    skos:scopeNote """Modal by design: asserts possibility in some context, not
        inevitability. Pair with mdcore:aggravatedByCondition to say when."""@en .

mdcore:mitigatedByDesignFeature a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "mitigated by design feature"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:FailureMode ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:DesignFeature .

mdcore:mitigatedFailureMode a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "failure mode mitigated by candidate"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:SubstitutionAssessment ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:FailureMode .

mdcore:modificationEffort a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "modification effort"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DesignModification ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    skos:scopeNote "Qualitative and analyst-assigned unless a source states otherwise; mark with mdcore:valueProvenance."@en .

mdcore:modificationStatement a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "modification statement"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DesignModification ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mdcore:modifiesInterface a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "modifies interface"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DesignModification ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:Interface .

mdcore:normalizedUnit a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "normalized unit"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:QuantityValue ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mdcore:normalizedValue a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "normalized value"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:QuantityValue ;
    rdfs:range xsd:decimal .

mdcore:numericValue a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "numeric value"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:QuantityValue ;
    rdfs:range xsd:decimal .

mdcore:ordinalRank a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "ordinal rank"@en ;
    rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
    skos:scopeNote """Ordering aid for queries. It is an ordinal, not a
        measurement: the gaps between ranks carry no meaning and ranks must not
        be averaged."""@en .

mdcore:originalUnit a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "original unit as printed"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:QuantityValue ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mdcore:originalValue a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "original value as printed"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:QuantityValue ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mdcore:partOf a owl:ObjectProperty,
        owl:TransitiveProperty ;
    rdfs:label "part of"@en ;
    owl:inverseOf mdcore:hasPart .

mdcore:performsFunction a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "performs function"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DesignAlternative ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:Function ;
    skos:definition """Relates a design alternative to a function it is capable
        of delivering. This is the entry point for the query 'what can perform
        this function?'."""@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Shared performsFunction is necessary but NOT sufficient
        for substitutability. See mdcore:SubstitutionAssessment."""@en .

mdcore:problemContext a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "problem operating context"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DesignProblem ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:OperatingContext .

mdcore:rangeMaximum a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "range maximum"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:QuantityValue ;
    rdfs:range xsd:decimal .

mdcore:rangeMinimum a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "range minimum"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:QuantityValue ;
    rdfs:range xsd:decimal .

mdcore:rationaleStatement a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "rationale statement"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DecisionRationale ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mdcore:realizesFunction a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "realizes function"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:Behavior ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:Function ;
    owl:inverseOf mdcore:realizedBy .

mdcore:rejectsAlternative a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "rejects alternative"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DesignDecision ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:DesignAlternative .

mdcore:reliesOnEffect a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "relies on physical effect"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:Behavior ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:PhysicalEffect .

mdcore:requiredDesignModification a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "required design modification"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:SubstitutionAssessment ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:DesignModification .

mdcore:requiredVerification a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "verification required before substituting"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:SubstitutionAssessment ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:VerificationMethod .

mdcore:requirementApplicableIn a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "requirement applicable in context"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:Requirement ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:OperatingContext .

mdcore:requirementStatement a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "requirement statement"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:Requirement ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mdcore:requiresAnalysis a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "requires analysis"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:FailureMode ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:VerificationMethod .

mdcore:requiresExternalAuthority a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "requires external authority"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:VerificationMethod ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:ExternalAuthorityKind .

mdcore:requiresFunction a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "requires function"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DesignProblem ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:Function .

mdcore:requiresInspection a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "requires inspection"@en ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:InspectionMethod .

mdcore:requiresTest a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "requires test"@en ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:TestMethod .

mdcore:reviewDate a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "review date"@en ;
    rdfs:range xsd:date .

mdcore:reviewStatus a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "review status"@en ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:ReviewState .

mdcore:reviewedBy a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "reviewed by"@en ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mdcore:ruleAppliesInContext a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "rule applies in context"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DesignRule ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:OperatingContext .

mdcore:ruleConcernsAlternative a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "rule concerns alternative"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DesignRule ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:DesignAlternative .

mdcore:ruleConcernsFunction a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "rule concerns function"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DesignRule ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:Function .

mdcore:ruleDerivedFromClaim a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "rule derived from claim"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DesignRule ;
    skos:scopeNote "Range is ev:Claim. A rule with no derived-from claim and no analyst attribution is unsupported."@en .

mdcore:ruleIdentifier a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "rule identifier"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DesignRule ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    skos:scopeNote "Must match the `id` of the corresponding entry in rules/*.yaml."@en .

mdcore:ruleIsAnalystAuthored a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "rule is analyst-authored"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DesignRule ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    skos:definition "True when the rule expresses ontology-engineering or engineering judgement rather than a cited source statement."@en .

mdcore:ruleStatement a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "rule statement"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DesignRule ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mdcore:satisfiedRequirement a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "requirement satisfied by candidate"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:SubstitutionAssessment ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:Requirement .

mdcore:selectsAlternative a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "selects alternative"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DesignDecision ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:DesignAlternative .

mdcore:sharesFunctionWith a owl:ObjectProperty,
        owl:SymmetricProperty ;
    rdfs:label "shares function with"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DesignAlternative ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:DesignAlternative ;
    skos:definition """Two alternatives can perform at least one common
        function. Symmetric, because co-function genuinely is symmetric --
        unlike substitutability, which is not."""@en .

mdcore:substitutionAssessedAs a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "substitution assessed as"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DesignAlternative ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:DesignAlternative ;
    skos:definition """A convenience shortcut from candidate to baseline,
        materialised by the build pipeline from an existing
        SubstitutionAssessment and never asserted by hand."""@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Explicitly NOT owl:SymmetricProperty and NOT
        owl:TransitiveProperty. Any reasoner configuration that makes it either
        is a misuse of this ontology."""@en .

mdcore:supportedByEvaluation a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "supported by evaluation"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:DecisionRationale ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:AlternativeEvaluation .

mdcore:testProcedureSpecified a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "test procedure specified by source"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:VerificationMethod ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    skos:scopeNote """False means the source did not define instruments, load
        levels, cycle counts or sequence. The ontology must not supply them."""@en .

mdcore:testRecommended a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "test recommended by source"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:VerificationMethod ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean .

mdcore:thresholdContext a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "threshold applies in context"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:ThresholdDefinition ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:OperatingContext .

mdcore:thresholdIsUniversal a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "threshold claimed universal by source"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:ThresholdDefinition ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    skos:scopeNote "Defaults to false. Set true only when the source explicitly presents the boundary as generally valid."@en .

mdcore:thresholdScopeNote a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "threshold scope note"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:ThresholdDefinition ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    skos:scopeNote "Records the limits the source itself placed on the boundary, e.g. that no sharp dividing line exists."@en .

mdcore:thresholdValue a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "threshold value"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:ThresholdDefinition ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:QuantityValue .

mdcore:tradeOffCosts a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "trade-off costs on criterion"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:TradeOff ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:EvaluationCriterion .

mdcore:tradeOffGains a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "trade-off gains on criterion"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:TradeOff ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:EvaluationCriterion .

mdcore:tradeOffStatement a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "trade-off statement"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:TradeOff ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mdcore:unitSymbol a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "unit symbol"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:QuantityValue ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    skos:scopeNote "Use 'dimensionless' for pure numbers such as a design factor."@en .

mdcore:usesEquation a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "uses equation"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:VerificationMethod ;
    skos:scopeNote "Range is ev:Equation, declared in the evidence module."@en .

mdcore:valueIsRange a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "value is a range"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:QuantityValue ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean .

mdcore:valueProvenance a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "value provenance"@en ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:ValueProvenanceKind ;
    skos:scopeNote "Required on every AlternativeEvaluation and on every numeric value that is not directly quoted from a source."@en .

mdcore:verifiedBy a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "verified by"@en ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:VerificationMethod ;
    skos:definition "Relates an alternative, requirement or failure mode to a method that checks it."@en .

mdcore:verifiesRequirement a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "verifies requirement"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:VerificationMethod ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:Requirement .

mdcore:violatedRequirement a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "requirement violated by candidate"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:SubstitutionAssessment ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:Requirement .

mdcore:yieldsSubFunction a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "yields sub-function"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mdcore:FunctionDecomposition ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:Function .

<https://w3id.org/mdkg/core/decision> a owl:Ontology ;
    dcterms:creator "mdkg ontology engineering (analyst-authored, not source-derived)"@en ;
    dcterms:title "mdkg core: design problem, alternatives and decisions"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "0.1.0" .

<https://w3id.org/mdkg/core/requirement> a owl:Ontology ;
    dcterms:creator "mdkg ontology engineering (analyst-authored, not source-derived)"@en ;
    dcterms:title "mdkg core: requirement, quantity and threshold"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "0.1.0" .

<https://w3id.org/mdkg/core/rule> a owl:Ontology ;
    dcterms:creator "mdkg ontology engineering (analyst-authored, not source-derived)"@en ;
    dcterms:title "mdkg core: design rules and review states"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "0.1.0" .

<https://w3id.org/mdkg/core/substitution> a owl:Ontology ;
    dcterms:creator "mdkg ontology engineering (analyst-authored, not source-derived)"@en ;
    dcterms:title "mdkg core: context-dependent substitution assessment"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "0.1.0" .

<https://w3id.org/mdkg/evidence> a owl:Ontology ;
    dcterms:creator "mdkg ontology engineering (analyst-authored, not source-derived)"@en ;
    dcterms:title "mdkg: evidence, provenance and claims"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "0.1.0" .

ev:BroaderThan a ev:AlignmentType ;
    skos:inScheme ev:AlignmentTypeScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "broader than"@en .

ev:CandidateDesignRule a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Candidate Design Rule"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ev:Claim ;
    skos:definition "A normalized claim proposed for promotion into the rule layer, not yet accepted."@en .

ev:ConflictingUsage a ev:AlignmentType ;
    skos:inScheme ev:AlignmentTypeScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "conflicting usage"@en .

ev:Contradicts a ev:AlignmentType ;
    skos:inScheme ev:AlignmentTypeScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "contradicts"@en .

ev:ExtractedClaim a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Extracted Claim"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ev:Claim ;
    skos:definition "A claim as first obtained from the source text, before normalisation."@en .

ev:ManufacturerCatalog a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Manufacturer Catalog"@en ;
    skos:altLabel "제조사 카탈로그"@ko ;
    skos:definition "A manufacturer's published data source, cited but not reproduced."@en .

ev:NarrowerThan a ev:AlignmentType ;
    skos:inScheme ev:AlignmentTypeScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "narrower than"@en .

ev:NotComparable a ev:AlignmentType ;
    skos:inScheme ev:AlignmentTypeScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "cannot be compared"@en .

ev:Unresolved a ev:AlignmentType ;
    skos:inScheme ev:AlignmentTypeScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "unresolved"@en .

ev:agreesWith a owl:ObjectProperty,
        owl:SymmetricProperty ;
    rdfs:label "agrees with"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Claim ;
    rdfs:range ev:Claim .

ev:alignmentType a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "alignment type"@en ;
    rdfs:range ev:AlignmentType .

ev:alignsSourceSymbol a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "source symbol"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:ConceptAlignment ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:alignsSourceTerm a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "source term"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:ConceptAlignment ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:alignsToConcept a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "aligns to core concept"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:ConceptAlignment .

ev:author a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "author"@en ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:blockIdentifier a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "paragraph or block identifier"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:EvidenceSpan ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:bookTitle a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "book title"@en ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:boundingBox a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "bounding box"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:EvidenceSpan ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    skos:scopeNote "PDF user-space coordinates as 'x0,y0,x1,y1', origin top-left, in points."@en .

ev:calculatedQuantity a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "calculated quantity"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Equation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:canonicalName a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "canonical name"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Variable ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:caption a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "caption"@en ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:chapterNumber a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "chapter number"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Chapter ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:chapterTitle a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "chapter title"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Chapter ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:claimAbout a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "claim is about"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Claim ;
    skos:definition """Links a claim to the ontology individual it concerns --
        an alternative, a function, a failure mode, a verification method.
        This is what lets a query walk from a design object to its
        evidence."""@en .

ev:claimAssumption a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "assumption"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Claim ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:claimCondition a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "condition stated by source"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Claim ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:claimException a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "exception stated by source"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Claim ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:claimIdentifier a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "claim identifier"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Claim ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:claimObject a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "claim object"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Claim ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:claimPredicate a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "claim predicate"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Claim ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:claimQuantity a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "quantitative value in claim"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Claim ;
    rdfs:range mdcore:QuantityValue .

ev:claimSubject a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "claim subject"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Claim ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:claimTopic a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "pilot topic"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Claim ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:commonConcept a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "common concept"@en ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:complements a owl:ObjectProperty,
        owl:SymmetricProperty ;
    rdfs:label "complements"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Claim ;
    rdfs:range ev:Claim .

ev:concernsEquation a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "concerns equation"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Claim ;
    rdfs:range ev:Equation .

ev:concernsFigure a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "concerns figure"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Claim ;
    rdfs:range ev:Figure .

ev:concernsTable a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "concerns table"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Claim ;
    rdfs:range ev:Table .

ev:contradicts a owl:ObjectProperty,
        owl:SymmetricProperty ;
    rdfs:label "contradicts"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Claim ;
    rdfs:range ev:Claim .

ev:differingAssumptions a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "differing assumptions"@en ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:differingConditions a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "differing conditions"@en ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:differsFrom a owl:ObjectProperty,
        owl:SymmetricProperty ;
    rdfs:label "differs from"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Claim ;
    rdfs:range ev:Claim .

ev:editionLabel a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "edition label"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:BookEdition ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:editionOf a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "edition of"@en ;
    owl:inverseOf ev:hasEdition .

ev:editionOrdinal a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "edition ordinal"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:BookEdition ;
    rdfs:range xsd:integer .

ev:equationAssumption a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "assumption"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Equation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:equationNumber a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "equation number"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Equation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:exampleNumber a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "example number"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:ExampleProblem ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:explainedBySpan a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "explained by surrounding text"@en ;
    rdfs:range ev:EvidenceSpan ;
    skos:definition """Links a table, figure or equation to the span of running
        text that explains it, so the item is never cited stripped of the
        conditions its own paragraph placed on it."""@en .

ev:extractedText a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "extracted text"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:EvidenceSpan ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:extractionConfidence a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "extraction confidence"@en ;
    rdfs:range xsd:decimal .

ev:extractionMethod a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "extraction method"@en ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    skos:scopeNote "For example 'pymupdf-1.24.11-textdict' or 'manual-transcription-from-rendered-page'."@en .

ev:figureNumber a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "figure number"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Figure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:fromSourceDocument a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "from source document"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Claim ;
    rdfs:range ev:SourceDocument .

ev:hasChapter a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has chapter"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:BookEdition ;
    rdfs:range ev:Chapter .

ev:hasDocument a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has source document"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:BookEdition ;
    rdfs:range ev:SourceDocument .

ev:hasInputVariable a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has input variable"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Equation ;
    rdfs:range ev:Variable .

ev:hasOutputVariable a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has output variable"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Equation ;
    rdfs:range ev:Variable .

ev:hasSection a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has section"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Chapter ;
    rdfs:range ev:Section .

ev:inChapter a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "in chapter"@en ;
    rdfs:range ev:Chapter .

ev:inSection a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "in section"@en ;
    rdfs:range ev:Section .

ev:localDefinition a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "local definition as given by the source"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Variable ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:mathFontCharRatio a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "math-font character ratio"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:EvidenceSpan ;
    rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
    skos:definition "Fraction of characters in the span set in a mathematics font; a machine-computed proxy for text-layer risk."@en .

ev:narrowerThanClaim a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "narrower than"@en ;
    owl:inverseOf ev:broaderThanClaim .

ev:normalizedStatement a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "normalized statement"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Claim ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:onPage a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "on page"@en ;
    rdfs:range ev:Page .

ev:originalExcerpt a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "short original excerpt"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Claim ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    skos:scopeNote "Kept deliberately short; the normalized statement carries the meaning."@en .

ev:pageCount a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "page count"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:SourceDocument ;
    rdfs:range xsd:integer .

ev:pageLabel a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "raw page label"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Page ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    skos:definition "The label exactly as declared by the PDF, including non-numeric labels such as 'Cover'."@en .

ev:pageLabelStyle a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "page label style"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Page ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    skos:scopeNote "One of 'arabic', 'roman', 'named', 'none'."@en .

ev:pageOfDocument a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "page of document"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Page ;
    rdfs:range ev:SourceDocument .

ev:pdfPageIndex a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "PDF page index (0-based)"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Page ;
    rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
    skos:definition """Zero-based index of the page within the PDF file, as
        used by PyMuPDF. The canonical machine-facing locator."""@en .

ev:pdfPageNumber a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "PDF page number (1-based)"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Page ;
    rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
    skos:definition "One-based page number as shown by a PDF viewer."@en .

ev:preferredUnit a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "preferred unit"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Variable ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:printedPage a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "printed page number"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Page ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    skos:definition """The page number printed on the page itself, taken from
        the PDF page-label tree. A string, because front matter is roman and
        some pages carry no number."""@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """MUST NOT be computed from pdfPageIndex. When absent, it is
        genuinely absent and the citation says so."""@en .

ev:publicationYear a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "publication year"@en ;
    rdfs:range xsd:gYear .

ev:publisher a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "publisher"@en ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:referencesFigure a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "references figure"@en ;
    rdfs:range ev:Figure .

ev:referencesTable a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "references table"@en ;
    rdfs:range ev:Table .

ev:refines a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "refines"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Claim ;
    rdfs:range ev:Claim .

ev:sectionNumber a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "section number"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Section ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:sectionTitle a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "section title"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Section ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:sha256 a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "SHA-256 of source file"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:SourceDocument ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:sourceClaimA a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "source claim A"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:ClaimAlignment ;
    rdfs:range ev:Claim .

ev:sourceClaimB a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "source claim B"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:ClaimAlignment ;
    rdfs:range ev:Claim .

ev:sourceFileName a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "source file name"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:SourceDocument ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:sourceNotation a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "source-specific notation"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Variable ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:spanOfDocument a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "span of document"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:EvidenceSpan ;
    rdfs:range ev:SourceDocument .

ev:spanOnPage a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "span on page"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:EvidenceSpan ;
    rdfs:range ev:Page .

ev:supportedByEvidence a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "supported by evidence"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Claim ;
    rdfs:range ev:Evidence .

ev:supports a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "supports"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Claim ;
    rdfs:range ev:Claim .

ev:symbol a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "symbol"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Variable ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:symbolicExpression a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "symbolic expression"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Equation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    skos:scopeNote """Transcribed by an analyst from the rendered page, not
        copied from the text layer, whenever ev:textIntegrity is not
        'reliable'. ev:transcriptionSource records which."""@en .

ev:tableNumber a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "table number"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Table ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:textIntegrity a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "text-layer integrity"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:EvidenceSpan ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    skos:definition """Assessment of whether the extracted characters faithfully
        represent the printed glyphs."""@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """One of 'reliable', 'partial-glyph-loss',
        'glyph-mismapped', 'unverified'. In the Shigley source, mathematics-font
        glyphs decode to unrelated ASCII characters, so spans covering
        equations are marked 'glyph-mismapped' and their text must not be
        quoted."""@en .

ev:transcriptionSource a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "transcription source"@en ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

ev:unitDimension a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "dimension"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Variable ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    skos:scopeNote "For example '[force]', '[length]', 'dimensionless'."@en .

ev:unitSystem a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "unit system required by equation"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Equation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    skos:scopeNote """Some printed equations are dimensionally inconsistent and
        valid only in the units the author assumed. Recording the required
        system prevents silent misuse in the other system."""@en .

ev:unresolvedRelativeTo a owl:ObjectProperty,
        owl:SymmetricProperty ;
    rdfs:label "unresolved relative to"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Claim ;
    rdfs:range ev:Claim .

ev:validityCondition a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "validity condition"@en ;
    rdfs:domain ev:Equation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

mdkg:SA-001 a mdcore:SubstitutionAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Replace a parallel key with an involute spline where the hub must slide under torque"@en ;
    mdcore:analystNote "Both books support the direction of this conclusion from different angles: Mott rules the key out for sliding service, Shigley rules the spline in. Neither book states the substitution as such; the conclusion is an analyst synthesis over two cited claims, and is marked NeedsReview."@en ;
    mdcore:applicableRequirement mdkg:req-axial-motion,
        mdkg:req-concentricity,
        mdkg:req-manufacturing-cost,
        mdkg:req-torque-capacity ;
    mdcore:assessmentAdvantage mdkg:SA-001_adv0,
        mdkg:SA-001_adv1,
        mdkg:SA-001_adv2 ;
    mdcore:assessmentConclusion mdcore:PreferredAlternative ;
    mdcore:assessmentCondition mdkg:SA-001_cond0,
        mdkg:SA-001_cond1 ;
    mdcore:assessmentContext mdkg:ctx-axial-slide-under-torque ;
    mdcore:assessmentDisadvantage mdkg:SA-001_dis0 ;
    mdcore:assessmentTradeOff mdkg:SA-001_to0 ;
    mdcore:baselineAlternative melem:ParallelKeyConnection ;
    mdcore:candidateAlternative melem:InvoluteSplineConnection ;
    mdcore:confidence 0.85 ;
    mdcore:functionBeingPreserved mech:TransmitTorqueShaftToHub ;
    mdcore:interfaceCompatibility mdcore:InterfaceCompatibleWithRework ;
    mdcore:introducedFailureMode mech:FatigueFracture,
        mech:WearOut ;
    mdcore:mitigatedFailureMode mech:FrettingWear,
        mech:ShearFailure ;
    mdcore:requiredDesignModification mdkg:SA-001_mod0,
        mdkg:SA-001_mod1,
