    ev:boundingBox "62.98,663.64,305.79,747.68" ;
    ev:extractedText "Where light loading and relatively easy assembly and disassembly are desired, the Woodruff key should be considered. Figure 11–3(e) shows the standard configuration. The circular groove in the shaft holds the key in position while the mating part is slid over the key. The stress analysis for this type of key proceeds in the manner discussed for the parallel key, taking into"@en ;
