mott6:es-0073 a ev:EvidenceSpan ;
    rdfs:label "mott6-es-0073" ;
    ev:blockIdentifier "mott6/p587/b12" ;
    ev:boundingBox "320.97,111.85,563.92,591.9" ;
    ev:extractedText "The basic static load rating, Co, is the load that the bearing can withstand without permanent deformation of any component. If this load is exceeded, the most probable result would be the indentation of one of the bearing races by the rolling elements. The deformation would be similar to that produced in the Brinell hardness test, and the failure is sometimes referred to as brinelling. Operation of the bearing after brinelling would be very noisy, and the impact loads on …"@en ;
    ev:extractionConfidence 0.95 ;
    ev:extractionMethod "pymupdf-textdict+anchor-verified" ;
    ev:inChapter mott6:ch_n14 ;
    ev:inSection mott6:sec_n14-7 ;
    ev:mathFontCharRatio 0.0 ;
    ev:spanOfDocument mott6:document ;
    ev:spanOnPage mott6:page_idx587 ;
    ev:textIntegrity "reliable" .

mott6:es-0074 a ev:EvidenceSpan ;
    rdfs:label "mott6-es-0074" ;
    ev:blockIdentifier "mott6/p586/b3" ;
    ev:boundingBox "308.98,709.58,551.79,757.62" ;
    ev:extractedText "Despite using steels with very high strength, all bearings have a finite life and will eventually fail due to fatigue because of the high contact stresses. But, obviously, the lighter the load, the longer the life, and vice versa. The"@en ;
    ev:extractionConfidence 0.95 ;
    ev:extractionMethod "pymupdf-textdict+anchor-verified" ;
    ev:inChapter mott6:ch_n14 ;
    ev:inSection mott6:sec_n14-6 ;
    ev:mathFontCharRatio 0.0 ;
