mott6:es-0040 a ev:EvidenceSpan ;
    rdfs:label "mott6-es-0040" ;
    ev:blockIdentifier "mott6/p495/b2" ;
    ev:boundingBox "320.98,70.93,563.92,358.98" ;
    ev:extractedText "A spline can be described as a series of axial keys machined into a shaft, with corresponding grooves machined into the bore of the mating part (gear, sheave, sprocket, and so on; see Figure 11–6). The splines perform the same function as a key in transmitting torque from the shaft to the mating element. The advantages of splines over keys are many. Because usually four or more splines are used, as compared with one or two keys, a more uniform transfer of the torque and a …"@en ;
    ev:extractionConfidence 0.95 ;
    ev:extractionMethod "pymupdf-textdict+anchor-verified" ;
    ev:inChapter mott6:ch_n11 ;
    ev:inSection mott6:sec_n11-5 ;
    ev:mathFontCharRatio 0.0 ;
