    ev:normalizedStatement "Shigley states that the Woodruff key yields better concentricity after assembly of wheel and shaft, especially important at high speeds, that it is useful when a wheel is positioned against a shoulder because the keyslot need not be machined into the shoulder stress-concentration region, and that its deeper penetration helps prevent key rolling in smaller shafts."@en ;
    ev:supportedByEvidence shigley10:es-0037 ;
    ev:textIntegrity "reliable" .

