    ev:textIntegrity "reliable" .

shigley10:es-0015 a ev:EvidenceSpan ;
    rdfs:label "shigley10-es-0015" ;
    mdcore:analystNote "Explicit condition ('low torque transmission') qualifying a set of alternatives."@en ;
    ev:blockIdentifier "shigley10/p379/b1" ;
    ev:boundingBox "238.5,98.35,589.01,457.51" ;
    ev:extractedText "Splines are essentially stubby gear teeth formed on the outside of the shaft and on the inside of the hub of the load-transmitting component. Splines are generally much more expensive to manufacture than keys, and are usually not necessary for simple torque transmission. They are typically used to transfer high torques. One feature of a spline is that it can be made with a reasonably loose slip fit to allow for large axial motion between the shaft and component while still …"@en ;
    ev:extractionConfidence 0.95 ;
    ev:extractionMethod "pymupdf-textdict+anchor-verified" ;
    ev:inChapter shigley10:ch_n7 ;
    ev:inSection shigley10:sec_n7-3 ;
    ev:mathFontCharRatio 0.0 ;
    ev:spanOfDocument shigley10:document ;
    ev:spanOnPage shigley10:page_idx379 ;
    ev:textIntegrity "reliable" .

shigley10:es-0034 a ev:EvidenceSpan ;
    rdfs:label "shigley10-es-0034" ;
    ev:blockIdentifier "shigley10/p405/b2" ;
    ev:boundingBox "238.5,455.95,589.03,647.11" ;
    ev:extractedText "The square key, shown in Fig. 7–16a, is also available in rectangular sizes. Standard sizes of these, together with the range of applicable shaft diameters, are listed in Table 7–6. The shaft diameter determines standard sizes for width, height, and key depth. The designer chooses an appropriate key length to carry the torsional load. Failure of the key can be by direct shear, or by bearing stress. Example 7–6 demonstrates the process to size the length of a key. The maximum …"@en ;
    ev:extractionConfidence 0.95 ;
    ev:extractionMethod "pymupdf-textdict+anchor-verified" ;
    ev:inChapter shigley10:ch_n7 ;
    ev:inSection shigley10:sec_n7-7 ;
    ev:mathFontCharRatio 0.0 ;
    ev:spanOfDocument shigley10:document ;
    ev:spanOnPage shigley10:page_idx405 ;
    ev:textIntegrity "reliable" .

